{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SuWXYFtnAMQ1xFz7n26XVq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue is in two places:\n\n1. `processChunk` at lines 158-166: `unicode.IsSpace(r)` non-space characters all increment `*lineLen`. But under GNU wc's C locale, only printable characters (0x20-0x7E for ASCII) contribute to line length. Non-printable chars should not increment `lineLen`.\n\n2. `processNonSpaceByte` at lines 180-188: The `default` case increments `*lineLen` for non-space bytes including control chars. Under C locale, control chars (< 0x20 or == 0x7F or > 0x7E) should not add to line length.\n\nWait, but I need to think about this more carefully. The GNU wc source uses `iswprint()` to decide if a character contributes to display width. Under `LC_ALL=C`:\n- 0x20-0x7E: printable, width 1\n- Everything else: not printable, width 0 (except tab which is handled separately)\n- Spaces (0x20) ARE printable and have width 1\n\nLet me also check how GNU wc handles space for -L:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":40099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e4478c1-354f-4f17-b93c-974fb4b35377","uuid":"cbafdbd9-cea3-4134-8de4-cce0c3d9bcfa"}
